       memory  object.   A  POSIX  shared  memory object is in effect a handle
       which can be used by unrelated processes to mmmmaapp(2) the same region  of
       shared  memory.  The sshhmm__uunnlliinnkk() function performs the converse opera‐
       tion, removing an object previously created by sshhmm__ooppeenn().

       The operation of sshhmm__ooppeenn() is analogous  to  that  of  ooppeenn(2).   _n_a_m_e
